# Local state, not source.

# The built sites. Every business renders into here, and GitHub Actions
# publishes it (.github/workflows/deploy.yml). It is thrown away and rebuilt on
# every build, so a copy in git could only ever be a stale one — which is
# exactly what it used to be, back when the built pages lived in the repo root.
dist/

# wrangler's own cache: which Cloudflare account you are logged into, and its
# build scratch. Machine-local, churns on every login and deploy.
worker/.wrangler/
.wrangler/

# npm, if a tool ever installs here
node_modules/

# The keys this machine holds and GitHub must never see. .env is where a token
# with real power lives (the Supabase personal access token, which may create
# and drop tables); .env.example is the empty shape of it and IS committed, so
# a new machine knows what to fill in. This repo is public and every change is
# pushed to main with `git add -A`, so the line below is load-bearing: see
# .githooks/pre-commit, which catches the same thing by content, in case this
# line is ever renamed out from under a file that still holds a key.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

